The problem with silver daggers is not the damage it's the population.
Silver daggers do silver damage so one silver dagger is better than
any one other type of dagger, but the primary strength of daggers is
they stack and multi-fire.  Who ever gets a stack of silver daggers?
Of course if you get one silver dagger it makes perfect sense to
wield it if you want to.

Elven daggers - 1 extra hit point compared to regular daggers, even
better against orcish daggers.

Elven daggers - Plentiful supply from elves and hobbits so at some
point in the game you'll have a dozen to fill your quiver.  Earlier in
the
game you get plenty of orcish daggers from orcs and then plenty
of daggers from gnomes and soldiers and so on.  Later in the game
you have plenty of elven.

Elven daggers - There's an artifact elven dagger that's trivial to
come by.

Elven daggers - They are made of wood so they are immune to rust
from the start.  Very good against black pudding, acidic monsters
and rust monsters.  They are subject to fire so switch to an iron
weapon when fighting brown puddings.


